# Backend & security (MUST)

- Authorize every request on the server (deny by default); row-level security on every user-data table with tests that user A can't access user B's data.
- Validate every input with a schema (Zod/Valibot); parameterized queries/ORM only; no `eval` or raw HTML from user data.
- Secrets only in server env vars; never in client code, logs, commits or error messages. Update `.env.example` with placeholder keys.
- Consistent error shape `{ error: { code, message } }` with correct status codes; fail closed; no stack traces to users.
- Rate limit auth, OTP, AI and other costly endpoints; idempotency keys for payments; verify webhook signatures.
- Migrations versioned in git; timestamps in UTC; indexes for filtered columns.
- Log security-relevant events without personal data. Minimum personal data; children's data needs verifiable parental consent.
- New dependency? State why, check it's real and maintained, and record it in `docs/product/DECISIONS.md`.

